  topic-grid/compact-quiz shape, vs. a2level's 4 of 11. One real asymmetry confirmed: NOT every
  compact-quiz chapter has a see-also block — as-datarepresent (ch.15) is compact-quiz with none,
  the only one of the 8 without a cross-reference row (7 see-also vs 8 compact-quiz chapters,
  confirmed exactly via grep before transcribing, not assumed).

  Several see-also links are genuinely cross-track (as-drv/as-bindist/as-normdist link into
  a2level's Continuous RVs/Poisson/Hypothesis-Testing chapters) — the existing seeAlsoBlock
  schema already supports a target trackId different from the current track (a2level's own
  Poisson chapter links back into aslevel's Binomial Distribution, confirming this is a real,
  intentional bidirectional cross-track reference network between the two A-Level tracks, not a
  one-off).

  No new block/tag shapes beyond what a2level introduced — chapterTag reuses 'category' with a
